1
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:11,900
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,967
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:43,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,300
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,233 --> 00:00:56,600
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,567 --> 00:00:59,233
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:00,567
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,000
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:03,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:07,100
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,767 --> 00:01:11,233
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:17,267
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,067
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:21,833
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:24,500
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:28,200
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:34,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,733 --> 00:01:35,933
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:37,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:38,833
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:40,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,867 --> 00:01:48,800
<i>Are we trying to pull
as many strings as we can</i>

24
00:01:48,933 --> 00:01:50,433
<i> here in the NCIA?</i>

25
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:52,100
<i>If I were to complete
the retraining,</i>

26
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:54,300
those groups might have already
come up with a plan against us!

27
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:56,467
<i>I order you not to dig into
the case any further.</i>

28
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:58,900
<i>Ma'am Sam, disobeying
Sir Delgado is dangerous.</i>

29
00:01:59,033 --> 00:02:01,067
<i>If that's what it takes,
I'll do it.</i>

30
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,600
<i> One for all. All for one.</i>

31
00:02:02,733 --> 00:02:04,300
<i> Her name is Samantha Jacinto.</i>

32
00:02:04,433 --> 00:02:06,700
<i>The youngest daughter
of the former NLEA chief.</i>

33
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:08,133
<i> She arrested Victor.</i>

34
00:02:08,267 --> 00:02:10,000
<i> We need to teach her a lesson.</i>

35
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:13,100
<i>Once I get out of here,
I'll collect you myself.</i>

36
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:14,967
<i>I'll get you
and your whole family!</i>

37
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:17,133
<i> We need money.</i>

38
00:02:17,267 --> 00:02:19,567
<i>Isn't Gabo doing everything
he can</i>

39
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,300
to be able to fund his father's
<i> operation?</i>

40
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:24,467
<i>I'm not coming back here
without any money.</i>

41
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:26,133
<i> We have a bigger problem.</i>

42
00:02:26,267 --> 00:02:28,900
<i> We'll take care of him.</i>

43
00:02:29,033 --> 00:02:32,067
<i>I was hoping to buy some
jewelry from you for my store.</i>

44
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,533
<i>I'll give you a big discount
today.</i>

45
00:02:33,667 --> 00:02:34,633
I'll meet you at the warehouse.

46
00:02:34,767 --> 00:02:35,800
<i> I really need your help.</i>

47
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:37,500
<i>Is there a mission
you can give me?</i>

48
00:02:37,633 --> 00:02:40,967
<i>You must take the gold
from Mr. Chan.</i>

49
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,767
I don't care if he dies or not.

50
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:49,333
Lucas.

51
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:53,200
Ma.

52
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:56,133
We're going to Mr. Chan.

53
00:02:57,367 --> 00:02:59,733
I'll take care of him myself.

54
00:02:59,867 --> 00:03:03,467
To make sure that the police
won't get anything out of him

55
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,633
- to use against Victor.
- [DEBORAH SIGHS]

56
00:03:05,767 --> 00:03:07,900
Do you really have
to come along?

57
00:03:08,233 --> 00:03:11,667
Just let your men
do all the work!

58
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:15,233
Let your son learn how to fight

59
00:03:15,367 --> 00:03:17,100
while Victor is gone.

60
00:03:18,233 --> 00:03:21,033
But there's a lot at stake here!

61
00:03:22,433 --> 00:03:23,867
What if he fails?

62
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,400
What will happen
to our business?

63
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,300
Lucas,

64
00:03:29,433 --> 00:03:33,867
we don't know how long your
brother will be in jail for.

65
00:03:35,167 --> 00:03:37,867
You're the only one
we can count on.

66
00:03:38,133 --> 00:03:40,567
Ma, this is nothing.

67
00:03:41,233 --> 00:03:42,500
I got this!

68
00:03:42,633 --> 00:03:44,033
- Arturo.
- Ma'am.

69
00:03:44,167 --> 00:03:45,767
- Go with them.
- Yes, ma'am.

70
00:03:47,767 --> 00:03:48,933
No need!

71
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:52,700
Ma,

72
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:55,033
I'm not a kid anymore.

73
00:03:55,367 --> 00:03:57,900
You no longer need to babysit
your son.

74
00:03:58,567 --> 00:04:00,267
He knows what he's doing.

75
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:05,433
Lucas, you better make sure
that you'll get rid of Mr. Chan.

76
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:06,867
Yes, Pa.

77
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:13,100
All of you.

79
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:14,433
Let's move!

80
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:21,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,667
- [CAR HORN HONKS]
- [ENGINE REVVING]

82
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:34,300
[SEBASTIAN] Thanks.

83
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:38,633
- [CHAIR CLATTERS]
- [OBJECTS RUSTLING]

84
00:04:38,767 --> 00:04:45,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:51,967
[CLICKS]

86
00:04:52,767 --> 00:04:53,867
[SEBASTIAN SIGHS]

87
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:56,100
Have you calmed down now?

88
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,500
Do you need something?

89
00:04:58,467 --> 00:04:59,533
Sam.

90
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:03,400
I know it's been a long day.

91
00:05:03,933 --> 00:05:06,533
I tried to give you
some space, but...

92
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,667
But no, I just can't win
against you.

93
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,967
So, please.

94
00:05:10,233 --> 00:05:13,433
Come with me. I even have
a restaurant reservation!

95
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:17,167
[INHALES SHARPLY]

96
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,433
Now's not really a good time.

97
00:05:18,567 --> 00:05:21,567
Maybe I could... indulge you
next time.

98
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Really? That's a promise!

99
00:05:24,667 --> 00:05:27,167
Yeah, just not right now,
alright? I'm quite busy.

100
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,833
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

101
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,167
It's a promise then. [LAUGHS]

102
00:05:37,633 --> 00:05:38,767
[DOOR OPENS]

103
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:40,233
[DOOR SLAMS CLOSE]

104
00:05:40,367 --> 00:05:44,933
Why did you let Lucas leave
without Arturo?

105
00:05:45,067 --> 00:05:50,700
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

106
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:52,100
[MARIANO GROANS]

107
00:05:52,733 --> 00:05:55,967
He's got a lot of men with him.
Don't worry.

108
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,633
Even so. It's still dangerous!

109
00:05:58,767 --> 00:06:02,800
And we cannot afford to risk it
especially with Victor gone!

110
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,300
[CHAIR CLATTERS]

111
00:06:10,233 --> 00:06:12,733
You grew up in this kind
of environment, Deborah.

112
00:06:12,867 --> 00:06:15,133
You know we have to take
risks and fight.

113
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:18,100
We'll never win
if we always hesitate.

114
00:06:18,667 --> 00:06:20,133
You said it yourself.

115
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,933
We should give Lucas a chance.

116
00:06:23,067 --> 00:06:24,833
Let him do his own thing.

117
00:06:25,533 --> 00:06:27,433
This is the perfect chance

118
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:29,500
for him to prove himself.

119
00:06:29,633 --> 00:06:36,600
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

120
00:06:45,267 --> 00:06:46,967
[DOOR OPENS]

121
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:48,533
[DOOR SLAMS CLOSE]

122
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:59,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:20,733
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:22,067
[ARTURO] Ma'am.

125
00:07:26,233 --> 00:07:27,933
Follow Lucas.

126
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,667
Find out what they're up to.

127
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,933
Protect him.

128
00:07:33,067 --> 00:07:35,600
Ma'am, is Sir Mariano
aware of this?

129
00:07:35,733 --> 00:07:38,533
Have you forgotten
where you've come from?

130
00:07:39,767 --> 00:07:42,533
Your father worked for my dad.

131
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,667
I just let Mariano have you.

132
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,633
But no matter what you have
achieved now

133
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:51,633
you owe it to me and my family.

134
00:07:51,767 --> 00:07:53,200
I know, ma'am.

135
00:07:53,933 --> 00:07:55,600
I'll go after Lucas now.

136
00:07:56,067 --> 00:07:57,900
If anything happens to my son,

137
00:07:58,267 --> 00:08:00,133
you'll be the one
who'll pay for it.

138
00:08:00,267 --> 00:08:07,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:20,100
Team, Ma'am Sam is here.

140
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:23,267
Team, are you ready?

141
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:24,333
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

142
00:08:24,467 --> 00:08:25,867
We'll capture Mr. Chan.

143
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,533
This time, he won't get away.

144
00:08:27,667 --> 00:08:28,767
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am.

145
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:30,333
- Let's go.
- Let's!

146
00:08:30,467 --> 00:08:32,000
[RALLOS] Hold it right there!

147
00:08:33,033 --> 00:08:34,233
Where are you going?

148
00:08:36,067 --> 00:08:37,300
Are you guys on a mission?

149
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:44,433
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:53,767
We just have somewhere to go.

151
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,100
Can I come?

152
00:08:55,267 --> 00:08:56,600
It's not like I'm an outsider.

153
00:08:56,733 --> 00:08:58,433
You can't come. Stay here.

154
00:08:58,567 --> 00:09:00,733
You'll really leave me behind?

155
00:09:01,133 --> 00:09:02,600
You won't give me something
before you go?

156
00:09:02,733 --> 00:09:04,200
Do you want me
to hit you before I go?

157
00:09:04,333 --> 00:09:06,833
Hey, Ernesto.
You'd better keep quiet!

158
00:09:06,967 --> 00:09:07,833
Zip it!

159
00:09:09,467 --> 00:09:10,467
Good boy.

160
00:09:12,067 --> 00:09:12,867
Let's go.

161
00:09:14,967 --> 00:09:15,800
Let's go.

162
00:09:15,933 --> 00:09:22,933
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,533
[SEBASTIAN] Rallos?

164
00:09:46,633 --> 00:09:47,733
Sir?

165
00:09:47,867 --> 00:09:50,567
Are you kidding me?
Are there other Rallos here?

166
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:51,567
Come here.

167
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:55,400
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

168
00:09:55,533 --> 00:09:57,100
- Sir?
- Where are they?

169
00:09:57,233 --> 00:09:58,633
Why aren't they here?

170
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,700
They're usually here
at this time.

171
00:10:03,233 --> 00:10:06,333
Sir, perhaps an order was given.

172
00:10:06,667 --> 00:10:09,933
Sam was in a hurry earlier.

173
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,333
I feel left out.

174
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:18,533
She's really giving me
a hard time.

175
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:22,600
Sir, if Ma'am Sam
is giving you a hard time,

176
00:10:22,733 --> 00:10:24,400
this is just a suggestion,

177
00:10:24,533 --> 00:10:27,733
but why don't you direct your
efforts towards Ma'am Pia.

178
00:10:27,867 --> 00:10:30,467
Do you want me to court her?

179
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,467
- She's not my type.
- [RALLOS] No, sir.

180
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:38,100
You'll gain Ma'am Pia's trust,

181
00:10:38,267 --> 00:10:40,933
that's when you'll praise
Ma'am Sam to her.

182
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:43,967
Hmm.

183
00:10:44,967 --> 00:10:47,333
To be honest,

184
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,867
she'll definitely listen to me.

185
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,167
I just need to figure her out.

186
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:56,967
Sir, just think about all
the brownie points you'll get.

187
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,700
Sam will more
likely say yes

188
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:01,767
if she finds out
you did that for her.

189
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:03,133
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

190
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:10,233
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:15,000
Pia?

192
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,800
Yes?

193
00:11:19,933 --> 00:11:24,467
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

194
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:27,400
You know what, Pia,
I just realized that...

195
00:11:27,533 --> 00:11:30,300
you need to have faith
in someone.

196
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,267
Meaning?

197
00:11:34,567 --> 00:11:35,500
Meaning...

198
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,400
You appreciate us agents.

199
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:43,467
[CHUCKLES] Well, Of course.

200
00:11:44,533 --> 00:11:50,400
My opinion is very
influential in this agency.

201
00:11:50,533 --> 00:11:52,433
I believe in that, Pia.

202
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:54,800
Pia.

203
00:11:55,667 --> 00:11:58,633
I hope you can
change your mind about Sam.

204
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,167
Let's give her
a second chance.

205
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,500
You know, you'll see her
in a different light.

206
00:12:05,767 --> 00:12:07,433
[SIGHS]

207
00:12:07,567 --> 00:12:10,433
Did Sam ask you to do this?

208
00:12:10,567 --> 00:12:11,900
Are you letting her use you?

209
00:12:12,033 --> 00:12:13,733
No. That's not the case.

210
00:12:15,167 --> 00:12:16,267
Pia.

211
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:20,933
Lately, I've noticed that Sam
has become more cranky.

212
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:25,867
But she's eager to solve
the gold smuggling case.

213
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,967
I think she's on to something.

214
00:12:28,667 --> 00:12:30,500
She's really paying attention
to this case.

215
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,067
Paying attention?

216
00:12:33,633 --> 00:12:35,333
Yes,
she's paying attention to it.

217
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:37,567
I just don't know why
she's not here now.

218
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:40,400
But usually,
at this time, she's here.

219
00:12:40,533 --> 00:12:43,133
She's really onto
this gold smuggling case.

220
00:12:43,267 --> 00:12:46,400
Let's just let her
prove herself.

221
00:12:46,533 --> 00:12:49,167
You'll be amazed.
Trust me.

222
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:56,367
[COMICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:13:05,533 --> 00:13:06,700
Hero.

224
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Good job, sir.

225
00:13:11,067 --> 00:13:12,533
Good job.

226
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,433
- [PIA] Sir.
- [DELGADO] Yes?

227
00:13:14,567 --> 00:13:18,967
It feels like your favorite
agent is being nosy.

228
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:20,767
What do you mean?

229
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:26,000
I think she's still
on to Tiger's case.

230
00:13:26,167 --> 00:13:28,667
- She disobeyed you.
- I already told her to stop.

231
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:31,900
I told her she was
hands off on this case.

232
00:13:32,033 --> 00:13:36,167
Well, it seems like
Sam has a point to prove.

233
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,967
Maybe my review
of her was right.

234
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:47,033
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

235
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:53,967
[WATER SPLASHES]

236
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:59,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

237
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:09,967
[ENGINE REVVING]

238
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,400
[DOOR CLICKS]

239
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:14,900
[DOOR SLAMS]

240
00:14:15,033 --> 00:14:19,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:14:19,633 --> 00:14:21,800
Hey, you! Do it faster!

242
00:14:21,933 --> 00:14:23,233
- Double time!
- [CLAPS]

243
00:14:23,367 --> 00:14:25,033
Double time!
Do it faster!

244
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:33,200
[ENGINE REVS]

245
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,000
Hey, you there!

246
00:14:36,133 --> 00:14:38,033
I want everything out today!

247
00:14:38,167 --> 00:14:39,433
Everything clean today!

248
00:14:39,567 --> 00:14:40,800
Double time! Double time!

249
00:14:40,933 --> 00:14:47,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

250
00:14:56,533 --> 00:14:57,500
[DOOR CLICKS]

251
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,867
[DOOR SLAMS]

252
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:07,667
[CASTOR] Team, let's stay here.

253
00:15:08,267 --> 00:15:09,733
Let's wait for them.

254
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:16,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

255
00:15:31,867 --> 00:15:38,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:15:44,267 --> 00:15:46,667
[METAL THUDS, CREAKS]

257
00:15:52,567 --> 00:15:53,300
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:15:53,433 --> 00:15:55,233
- [UMALI] Sir.
- [DOMINGO] Yes?

259
00:15:56,833 --> 00:15:57,767
Sir.

260
00:15:59,567 --> 00:16:02,200
I have relayed your message
to Paquito.

261
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:05,467
Good. I'm expecting
better news tomorrow.

262
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,900
Sir, I was just thinking.

263
00:16:08,067 --> 00:16:10,367
Maybe we could have
other people do the job.

264
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,933
I agree, sir.

265
00:16:12,067 --> 00:16:13,667
They're full of themselves.

266
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,533
They act as if they are
the law.

267
00:16:15,667 --> 00:16:17,033
Especially that Django.

268
00:16:17,167 --> 00:16:18,833
Sir, let's just get rid
of them.

269
00:16:18,967 --> 00:16:20,667
I know other people
who can do the job.

270
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:23,900
Umali, we've been working with
Paquito for a while now.

271
00:16:24,033 --> 00:16:25,767
I trust their group.

272
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:29,033
Just ignore their rude behavior.

273
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:31,500
I mean, they're criminals,
remember?

274
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:33,400
If you say so, sir.

275
00:16:35,633 --> 00:16:38,567
What matters is that we
get rid of our problem.

276
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,467
Salvador will be gone.

277
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:45,033
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:16:46,267 --> 00:16:49,100
[DJANGO] We got a high-paying
job for tomorrow.

279
00:16:49,233 --> 00:16:50,300
That's easy, boss.

280
00:16:50,433 --> 00:16:53,533
Does it involve beating someone
up or stealing?

281
00:16:55,033 --> 00:16:56,600
[SALVADOR ON TV]
<i> After the interview...</i>

282
00:16:56,733 --> 00:17:00,267
We'll rob, threaten him,
and beat him up.

283
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:02,067
He's our target.

284
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:05,633
- A mediocre news reporter.
<i> - Someone got hospitalized.</i>

285
00:17:05,767 --> 00:17:07,600
<i>Is it necessary to get
someone hurt?</i>

286
00:17:07,733 --> 00:17:09,967
Boss, he interviewed
Miss Betchay

287
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,733
and did a report
on Mister Rudy.

288
00:17:11,867 --> 00:17:13,600
That's why we need
to teach him a lesson

289
00:17:13,733 --> 00:17:15,033
and keep his mouth shut.

290
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,167
It's a piece of cake, boss.

291
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:18,867
I know, it's not even
challenging.

292
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,133
I'll do the job without
breaking a sweat.

293
00:17:21,267 --> 00:17:22,833
[LAUGHTER]

294
00:17:22,967 --> 00:17:24,667
You all got this, right?

295
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:26,533
- [HENCHMAN 1] Of course.
- Django.

296
00:17:26,667 --> 00:17:29,333
- [SALVADOR ON TV]<i> Once again...
</i>- Django.

297
00:17:29,467 --> 00:17:31,467
<i>I am Salvador "The Vindicator"
Manalo,</i>

298
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,267
<i> supporter of the oppressed.</i>

299
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,367
- Yes, Pa?
- Listen, Django.

300
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:39,700
Don't underestimate this job.

301
00:17:39,833 --> 00:17:41,933
Whether it involves a big-time
person or not,

302
00:17:42,067 --> 00:17:44,900
you should treat them
equally.

303
00:17:45,567 --> 00:17:46,800
Okay, Pa.

304
00:17:46,933 --> 00:17:49,467
Umali paid us a huge amount
for this job,

305
00:17:49,633 --> 00:17:54,467
so it'd be best that you
do it yourself.

306
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:57,133
Umali could've hired
other people,

307
00:17:57,267 --> 00:17:59,967
but he entrusted it
to us.

308
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:04,433
So, we must not get
complacent.

309
00:18:04,567 --> 00:18:07,833
We can't have them
lose their trust in us.

310
00:18:07,967 --> 00:18:12,700
Besides, we need protection
from the police.

311
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:13,933
Why?

312
00:18:14,533 --> 00:18:17,333
They also need us, so that
makes us even. Right, Pa?

313
00:18:17,467 --> 00:18:21,300
We need them more than
they need us,

314
00:18:21,467 --> 00:18:24,733
so you have to do
the job well.

315
00:18:25,567 --> 00:18:28,367
Do the job that they
want us to do.

316
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,633
Okay, Pa.
Leave it to me.

317
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:36,800
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:18:36,933 --> 00:18:39,033
- Rallos.
- Sir.

319
00:18:41,533 --> 00:18:43,200
Where are the others?

320
00:18:43,333 --> 00:18:44,533
Where did they go?

321
00:18:45,433 --> 00:18:46,333
I don't know, sir.

322
00:18:46,467 --> 00:18:47,733
- Tuazon.
- Sir.

323
00:18:47,867 --> 00:18:49,533
Do you know where
the others are?

324
00:18:49,667 --> 00:18:50,933
Sir, I have no idea.

325
00:18:51,067 --> 00:18:52,400
- Yeah, right.
- Do you need anything, sir?

326
00:18:52,533 --> 00:18:53,700
You're obviously lying.

327
00:18:53,833 --> 00:18:57,433
You said that Jacinto
seems focused

328
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,600
on the gold smuggling
case, right?

329
00:18:59,733 --> 00:19:02,167
That's not what I meant,
Ma'am Pia.

330
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:06,000
What I'm trying to say is that
Sam is worried about it.

331
00:19:06,133 --> 00:19:07,367
That's all.

332
00:19:09,467 --> 00:19:12,033
[WHISPERING] They left to deal
with a gold smuggling case?

333
00:19:13,133 --> 00:19:14,567
Rallos!

334
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:16,900
Do you know anything
about what they're doing?

335
00:19:17,033 --> 00:19:17,967
N--No, sir.

336
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:19,667
- I was just thinking...
- [DELGADO] What?

337
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:22,800
If they went some place,
it's possible they went there.

338
00:19:22,933 --> 00:19:23,967
Where?

339
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:28,867
This is gross insubordination!

340
00:19:29,033 --> 00:19:31,800
They are acting
without my permission!

341
00:19:31,933 --> 00:19:34,933
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

342
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:38,467
I want everything out
today, okay?

343
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:41,267
Put all my stocks
in the truck.

344
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,900
- Clear?
- Yes, boss.

345
00:19:43,033 --> 00:19:44,433
[PHONE RINGING]

346
00:19:45,067 --> 00:19:47,000
- Hello?
- Hi, Mr. Chan.

347
00:19:47,133 --> 00:19:48,133
It's Carlota.

348
00:19:48,267 --> 00:19:49,933
Yes. Yes, I remember you.

349
00:19:50,067 --> 00:19:51,300
Beautiful girl, yes.

350
00:19:51,433 --> 00:19:52,833
Yes. I'm here outside
the building.

351
00:19:52,967 --> 00:19:55,000
You come inside.
I'll wait for you here.

352
00:19:55,133 --> 00:19:56,500
[CALL DROPS]

353
00:19:56,633 --> 00:20:03,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:20:04,433 --> 00:20:06,033
- Good evening, ma'am.
- Good evening.

355
00:20:06,167 --> 00:20:08,600
We have a meeting
with Mr. Chan

356
00:20:08,733 --> 00:20:10,067
to purchase some
jewelry.

357
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:12,033
Okay. I'll accompany you
to him.

358
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,233
[DELGADO] Rallos, call Limbaga.

359
00:20:15,367 --> 00:20:16,467
Sir, why me?

360
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,867
Why you? Aren't you two close?

361
00:20:20,233 --> 00:20:21,867
[WHISPERING] Call her now.

362
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,633
Really? Me?

363
00:20:23,767 --> 00:20:25,133
[SEBASTIAN] Why aren't
you calling her?

364
00:20:25,267 --> 00:20:26,633
Are you hiding something?

365
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:27,767
No, sir.

366
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:30,333
If I knew, I would've joined
them in their mission.

367
00:20:31,267 --> 00:20:32,900
That is, if they are
on a mission.

368
00:20:33,033 --> 00:20:34,033
[PIA] Sir.

369
00:20:35,267 --> 00:20:37,400
I found Mr. Chan's
calling card.

370
00:20:38,267 --> 00:20:41,533
I think this is where
they went.

371
00:20:46,933 --> 00:20:49,200
Sam pursued the case even though
I told her to stop.

372
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:52,833
I'm not going to let anyone
ignore my orders

373
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:56,000
here in NCIA!

374
00:20:56,133 --> 00:21:03,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

375
00:21:07,233 --> 00:21:12,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

376
00:21:12,233 --> 00:21:14,467
Alright. Jacinto is in.

377
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:17,100
Let's just wait
for her go signal.

378
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:19,233
I have a bad feeling about this.

379
00:21:19,367 --> 00:21:21,367
This place looks dangerous.

380
00:21:22,367 --> 00:21:29,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

381
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:48,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

382
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:57,900
Mr. Chan.

383
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:02,133
I'm Carlota.
We talked on the phone.

384
00:22:02,267 --> 00:22:03,600
We're the ones who'll buy
jewelry from you.

385
00:22:03,733 --> 00:22:06,533
Yes, I remember you.
Beautiful girl.

386
00:22:07,733 --> 00:22:14,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:22:19,033 --> 00:22:24,967
- [DARK MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ENGINES REVVING]

388
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:36,000
Sorry, we're doing business here
today. My shop is closed.

389
00:22:36,133 --> 00:22:37,867
It's really hot.
Want some water?

390
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,933
Oh... It's okay.

391
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:43,867
Wait, you said you're closed.
Why are you closed?

392
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,567
None of your business.

393
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:48,567
You're very beautiful.

394
00:22:48,733 --> 00:22:51,500
Last time, I didn't
notice since I was busy.

395
00:22:51,633 --> 00:22:52,900
Now I see how pretty you are.

396
00:22:53,033 --> 00:22:54,000
[KAREN CHUCKLES]

397
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:58,333
Mr. Chan, do you think
I'm beautiful, too?

398
00:22:58,467 --> 00:23:01,567
Oh! Sorry about that. My friend
here is just a big joker.

399
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:03,900
This is Jessica. She's my
partner in this business.

400
00:23:04,033 --> 00:23:05,100
Mr. Chan.

401
00:23:08,033 --> 00:23:12,600
Sir, is there any way you
could give us a huge discount?

402
00:23:12,733 --> 00:23:15,033
We're buying in bulk anyway.

403
00:23:15,167 --> 00:23:16,667
Beautiful girl, no problem.

404
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:19,533
- I'll give you a 70% discount.
- Mm.

405
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:25,433
Uh... Sir, I noticed you have
an attaché case there.

406
00:23:25,567 --> 00:23:28,200
Do you have jewelry inside?
Can we take a look?

407
00:23:28,333 --> 00:23:30,967
It holds gold bars.
Want a gold bar?

408
00:23:31,100 --> 00:23:34,100
I'll give you gold bars
at 70% off, too.

409
00:23:34,233 --> 00:23:36,600
Go on a date with me.
Let's fly to China!

410
00:23:36,733 --> 00:23:38,800
We'll shop
and I will pay for everything!

411
00:23:38,933 --> 00:23:42,733
Carlota, say yes! Think of
how much money we'll make!

412
00:23:42,867 --> 00:23:45,500
Plus, he's practically
giving it away, right?

413
00:23:45,633 --> 00:23:46,533
[CHUCKLES]

414
00:23:46,667 --> 00:23:48,933
Oh, come on.
We came here for business.

415
00:23:49,067 --> 00:23:51,600
We do business, no dates.

416
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:59,733
[ENGINES REVVING]

417
00:23:59,867 --> 00:24:01,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

418
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:03,733
[CAR DOORS OPEN]

419
00:24:03,867 --> 00:24:07,567
[GUNSHOTS]

420
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:08,667
Who are they?!

421
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:11,967
[GUNSHOTS CONTINUE]

422
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:13,767
- What's that? What's that?
- Mr. Chan!

423
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:15,767
Enemies are attacking!

424
00:24:15,900 --> 00:24:17,600
Hey, check everything!
Double check it!

425
00:24:17,733 --> 00:24:20,067
<i>- Reyes, hurry, get inside!
- Let's go!</i>

426
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

427
00:24:23,533 --> 00:24:30,367
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

428
00:24:44,867 --> 00:24:51,700
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [GUNSHOTS CONTINUE]

429
00:24:52,767 --> 00:24:54,133
[ROPE CINCHING TIGHT]

430
00:24:54,267 --> 00:24:58,233
- [ROPE ZIPPING ALONG LINE]
- [THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

431
00:24:58,367 --> 00:24:59,833
[BLOWS LAND]

432
00:24:59,967 --> 00:25:01,900
- [KICKS LAND]
- [GRUNTS LOUDLY]

433
00:25:03,533 --> 00:25:06,467
- [SLINGSHOT STRETCHING, TWANGS]
- [GUNSHOTS]

434
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:08,267
[GRUNTS, KICK LANDS]

435
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:12,967
[GUNSHOTS]

436
00:25:13,100 --> 00:25:15,267
- [BODY THUDS]
- [KICK LANDS]

437
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:18,300
- [SLINGSHOT TWANGS]
- [ENGINE REVVING]

438
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:22,300
[GUNSHOTS CONTINUE]

439
00:25:22,433 --> 00:25:27,200
[GRUNTING LOUDLY]

440
00:25:27,333 --> 00:25:33,667
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

441
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:35,900
[KICKS LAND]

442
00:25:36,067 --> 00:25:38,900
[SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

443
00:25:39,033 --> 00:25:43,733
Spread out! We're wiping out
Mr. Chan's men!

444
00:25:43,867 --> 00:25:45,000
[YELLS] Ah!

445
00:25:45,133 --> 00:25:52,000
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [GUNSHOTS]

446
00:25:55,967 --> 00:25:58,600
[MEN GROANING IN PAIN]

447
00:25:58,733 --> 00:26:05,600
- [SLINGSHOT TWANGS]
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

448
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,367
[SLINGSHOT STRETCHING]

449
00:26:09,533 --> 00:26:16,433
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC SWELLS]

450
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:24,133
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [BLOWS LAND]

451
00:26:24,267 --> 00:26:25,300
[BODY THUDS]

452
00:26:25,433 --> 00:26:26,733
- [PUNCHES AND KICKS LANDING]
- [GLASS SHATTERING]

453
00:26:26,867 --> 00:26:30,633
<i>Victor's freedom rests
in Lucas's hands.</i>

454
00:26:30,767 --> 00:26:33,367
<i>I'll do whatever it takes
to save my brother!</i>

455
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:35,467
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [PUNCHES AND KICKS LANDING]

456
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,667
[GRUNTING LOUDLY]

457
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:41,800
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [KICK LANDS]

458
00:26:41,967 --> 00:26:43,100
- [GROANS IN PAIN]
<i> - Let's go!</i>

459
00:26:43,233 --> 00:26:45,767
[KICKS LAND, THWACKING]

460
00:26:45,900 --> 00:26:50,133
Will Gabo finally
succeed in his mission?

461
00:26:50,267 --> 00:26:52,467
<i>- Mr. Chan!
- We need our car right now!</i>

462
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:55,667
Or face a whole
new set of challenges?

463
00:26:56,867 --> 00:26:59,833
<i> Freeze! NCIA! Nobody move!</i>
